// English interface text → [Kiswahili, Sheng].
//
// Kiswahili: correct, plain Kiswahili as used in Kenya (dawa, dozi, homa).
// Sheng: the casual Nairobi / Gen Z mix young Kenyans text in.
// Legal and consent wording uses the Kiswahili text in both, so nothing
// legal depends on slang (S(...) below). Danger signs and medicine
// instructions stay plain in both.
//
// Keys must match the English on screen exactly (spaces collapsed).
// Text with a name or number in it goes in PATTERNS at the bottom.

